            {
                "entry_id": "a7e1a422-76fe-3b39-8fb4-8f8fc77b4b2a",
                "word": "DIU",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "04cd057f-0d54-35c8-ad14-ed6e0ff2ffed",
                        "entry_id": "a7e1a422-76fe-3b39-8fb4-8f8fc77b4b2a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Stérilet, dispositif intra-utérin."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "47c10890-8d99-4d77-936b-c9475708a228",
                                "sense_id": "04cd057f-0d54-35c8-ad14-ed6e0ff2ffed",
                                "text": "Longtemps réservé aux femmes ayant déjà eu des enfants, le DIU peut aujourd’hui être proposé aux nullipares."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "adcc1991-44f5-4b6f-8cd3-283129dc6788",
                                "sense_id": "04cd057f-0d54-35c8-ad14-ed6e0ff2ffed",
                                "text": "Retraçant le cheminement qui l’a amenée à ne pas faire d’enfant, l’écrivaine Pam Houston évoque, elle, l'influence de sa professeure d'études féministes à l'université de Denison (Ohio) en 1980, Nan Nowik, qui, « grande, élégante », portait des DIU en guise de boucles d'oreilles."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "2c88ac0c-5733-3249-abbd-d0ae87c0efc1",
                        "entry_id": "a7e1a422-76fe-3b39-8fb4-8f8fc77b4b2a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Droit irrévocable d’usage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": []
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "64520742-0d32-4177-a663-16cbae7ce33e",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7e1a422-76fe-3b39-8fb4-8f8fc77b4b2a",
                        "target_lang_word": "intrauterine device",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "intrauterine device",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5581fb80-b452-3ddc-98c3-c2b114e01b4f",
                                        "entry_id": "bcdf8bf5-805b-3562-8625-3b223ac09f00",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A contraceptive device consisting of a spiral or similar shape of plastic or metal inserted through the vagina into the uterus in order to prevent the implantation of a fertilized egg."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "72fa414e-fd98-4238-90c7-51b4c3e84b98",
                                                "sense_id": "5581fb80-b452-3ddc-98c3-c2b114e01b4f",
                                                "text": "Types of progestagen-only contraceptives available in the UK and US include the implant, the hormonal intrauterine device (IUD), the contraceptive injection and the minipill."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "20541409-b0b2-4f21-aca7-4cc062e96dd4",
                                                "sense_id": "5581fb80-b452-3ddc-98c3-c2b114e01b4f",
                                                "text": "The latest research, published Wednesday in the medical journal JAMA, analyzed years of health records for thousands of Danish women ages 15 to 49, with an even split between those who started using intrauterine devices that release the hormone levonorgestrel for birth control and those who hadn’t used any type of hormonal contraceptive."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "0e7fa1d3-079d-474a-b4f4-30c67157f4bb",
                        "source_entry_id": "a7e1a422-76fe-3b39-8fb4-8f8fc77b4b2a",
                        "target_lang_word": "IUD",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "IUD",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "0fe78336-b3bf-3850-89c5-aba63d550c6b",
                                        "entry_id": "996671df-84b0-3ea0-81d7-59f2dad85770",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of intrauterine device."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84463c0e-7dca-4bde-ab31-90c5244d8f2a",
                                                "sense_id": "0fe78336-b3bf-3850-89c5-aba63d550c6b",
                                                "text": "An IUD is a type of long-acting, reversible contraceptive. The small, T-shaped device is placed in the uterus and left in place to prevent pregnancy for between three and 12 years, depending on the type."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9f595228-0d02-4851-9043-05a00bdccdc8",
                                                "sense_id": "0fe78336-b3bf-3850-89c5-aba63d550c6b",
                                                "text": "That, and her IUD, which had become so deeply embedded in her uterine lining that only the uninsured process of surgical extraction could remove it, had created a false narrative of childlessness."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4c940463-53eb-4350-a8cc-c15ff4230706",
                                                "sense_id": "0fe78336-b3bf-3850-89c5-aba63d550c6b",
                                                "text": "The authors also said they attempted to investigate whether there are differing breast cancer risks between hormonal and nonhormonal IUDs. However, they said too few women in England had been prescribed nonhormonal IUDs to make a reliable comparison."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88a48dde-d9d9-4555-87fa-cae391342b90",
                                                "sense_id": "0fe78336-b3bf-3850-89c5-aba63d550c6b",
                                                "text": "For Dr. Eleanor Bimla Schwarz, professor of medicine at the University of California, San Francisco, the benefits of an IUD far outweigh the risks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "33bf1c7d-5699-3841-b40b-ad2c0067bcf4",
                                        "entry_id": "996671df-84b0-3ea0-81d7-59f2dad85770",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Initialism of inhalant use disorder."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "alt-of",
                                            "countable",
                                            "initialism",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ecc3de0-7d1f-45a0-ace4-51713085c431",
                                                "sense_id": "33bf1c7d-5699-3841-b40b-ad2c0067bcf4",
                                                "text": "Typically, respondents with ASPD that use inhalants often exhibited a greater level of antisocialism, and this relationship was intensified further if the inhalant user had an IUD."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3bb0fc42-24f7-3bef-8bad-43234a69580f",
                                        "entry_id": "996671df-84b0-3ea0-81d7-59f2dad85770",
